          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Deoran",
            text: _("If only Ethiliel had not fled! I curse our isolation, so far removed from the great cities of the north. The capital garrison alone would make short work of this lich, if only we could have contacted them in time!"),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_115",
        on: "turn",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "condition",
            variable: "turn_number",
            equals: 4,
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Mebrin",
            text: _("The shroud of darkness descends once more. Night seeps through the cracks and crannies in the humans’ defenses, plaguing their minds and bodies with dreadful fear. As surely as the sanctity of the psyche is shattered, so is the physical form, and all that’s left is unthinking, unfeeling servitude."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Deoran",
            text: _("We don’t fear your unholy power, lich. We won’t succumb to your dark magics and we won’t be turned into your undead slaves."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Mebrin",
            text: _("Believe what you will, human. We shall see if you survive the night."),
          },
        ],
      },
